1: //! The `exec` role (P5-T1): a JSON-RPC `initialize` handshake over
2: //! stdin/stdout, followed by a Landlock-sandboxed `exec` of the target command
3: //! described by an [`ExecPlan`].
4: //!
5: //! Protocol (one JSON object per line):
6: //! 1. stdin line 1 — `initialize` request. `params.protocolVersion` MUST equal
7: //!    [`openbuff_workspace_harness::workspace_protocol_version`] (single source
8: //!    of truth; never hardcoded here). On match we reply with a JSON-RPC
9: //!    `result` line on stdout; on mismatch (or malformed/wrong-method) we reply
10: //!    with a JSON-RPC `error` object (`code: -32600`) on stdout and exit 1.
11: //! 2. stdin line 2 — the [`ExecPlan`] as JSON. We apply the Landlock ruleset
12: //!    (Linux only) and then `exec` the target, replacing this process.
13: //!
14: //! Exit-code contract: any failure before `exec` (EOF, malformed plan, bad
15: //! handshake, landlock/exec error) emits a one-line JSON envelope and exits 1.
16: 
